{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For</b> — He will hide me, and no enemy will be able to touch me." "<b>In a booth</b> — that is Jerusalem, as in: 'and in Salem was His booth' (Psalms 76:3)." "<b>On the day of evil</b> — an evil alignment of stars against his sign." "And the sense of <b>in the Rock</b> — for I will be in the shelter of His tent, as though I were in a high rocky fastness."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:41.814202671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}